E={
156:dict(n="Blood on the Clocktower",s="Large social deduction game run by a Storyteller: good players hunt the Demon; every role is unique, the dead stay in the game with one ghost vote, and drunk or poisoned players may get false information.",
su=["The Storyteller picks a script (Trouble Brewing for beginners, 5–15 players) and builds the character mix by player count (e.g. 7 players: 5 Townsfolk, 0 Outsiders, 1 Minion, 1 Demon).","Players sit in a circle and secretly draw unique character tokens; the Storyteller records seats and roles in the Grimoire.","The Drunk is given a Townsfolk token and does not know they are the Drunk."],
t=["First night: with 7+ players the Minions and Demon learn each other; the Demon learns 3 good characters not in play to bluff as; first-night characters receive information in order.","Day: deaths are announced (roles stay hidden); open and private discussion.","Nominations: only living players nominate, once per day each, and each player can be nominated once per day; votes of at least half the living players put someone on the block; a later nominee needs more votes to replace them; a tie means no execution.","At most one execution per day; then night falls. Each later night the Demon kills and other characters act in order."],
e=["Good wins when the Demon dies (and no new Demon is created, e.g. by the Scarlet Woman).","Evil wins when only 2 players are alive and the Demon lives, or via special conditions such as the Saint being executed.","The dead win or lose with their team."],
tp=["Cross-check information: you might be poisoned or the Drunk.","Good players share information early; evil players prepare a bluff.","Do not go quiet after death — ghost votes often decide the final day.","Start new groups on Trouble Brewing."],
pf=["Dead players cannot nominate and have only one ghost vote for the whole game.","A tied vote executes no one.","You need a Storyteller who knows the rules well."]),
157:dict(n="Blade's Rose",s="Everyone holds 3 role cards — any red card makes you a Blade. Each round players secretly add cards to the ritual; if a blade is revealed, the white cards are killed; the White Rose revealed with a blade means instant Blade victory.",
su=["Use the player board and role cards for the player count; deal 3 role cards to each player and set centre cards per the rules.","Hand out the White Crystal spell cards as the rulebook says.","Night: eye-icon roles (White Rose, Bishop, Twin Blade, Great Blade) wake in order; the Twin Blade may swap the Ghost with the centre Twin Blade."],
t=["The coin holder passes the gold coin to a player who still has crystals; that player reveals and resolves one crystal.","From the coin holder, each player in order may play one role card face down (or pass).","Shuffle the played cards and reveal; discard any Ghost.","If any blade is revealed, all revealed white cards go to the kill area; otherwise they go to the sacrifice area."],
e=["White Rose revealed together with a blade: the Blades win instantly.","White wins if the White Rose has been played safely and sacrifices reach the board threshold before the final round.","Blades win on reaching the kill threshold, or when the final round ends without a White victory."],
tp=["The White Rose should go in on a round that looks clean.","Passing is information too.","Blades can play white cards first to look innocent."],
pf=["Your team depends on all 3 cards in hand.","A revealed Ghost is simply discarded.","The sacrifice threshold must be reached before the final round."]),
158:dict(n="I'm the Boss 3: Merger Tycoon",s="Another card game in the Chinese \"I'm the Boss\" line: run companies, trade shares, mergers and shareholder dividends. Only a video rules explanation exists online — follow the rulebook.",
su=["Set up per the rulebook (the video lists: setup, choosing the first player)."],
t=["Player actions as described in the rulebook.","Company operations and mergers.","Company bankruptcy and shareholder dividends; handling several mergers triggered at once."],
e=["Win per the rulebook (most money is likely, but check)."],
tp=["Play one open-handed practice round to walk through a merger payout.","Watch who is hoarding shares of the same company."],
pf=["It is a different game from I'm the Boss (doc 100); do not mix rules.","Do not use Acquire's numbers."]),
159:dict(n="Betrayal at House on the Hill 3rd Edition",s="Explore a haunted house together; omens build up until the haunt starts, then a scenario reveals a traitor or special situation and each side follows secret goals. 50 haunts.",
su=["Place the 3 starting tiles; shuffle the other room tiles.","Each player takes a character and sets Might, Speed, Sanity and Knowledge to their start values.","Separate Event, Item and Omen cards; choose a Scenario card (it decides which haunt and who the traitor is)."],
t=["Move up to your Speed; discovering a new room ends your turn immediately (3rd-edition rule).","Room symbols: draw an Event, Item or Omen.","Haunt roll: after each Omen, roll as many dice as Omens revealed; 5 or more starts the haunt; the last Omen always starts it.","After the haunt: read the introduction and setup aloud, then traitor and heroes read their own secret goals separately."],
e=["The side that completes its haunt goal wins.","Monsters are usually only stunned, not killed, unless the haunt says otherwise."],
tp=["Collect items before the haunt.","Track omens to predict when the haunt arrives.","Heroes should split tasks quickly."],
pf=["Draw cards only when a room is first revealed.","No one can die before the haunt.","Stealing items is off by default in 3rd edition."]),
160:dict(n="Warhammer Quest: The Adventure Card Game",s="Fully co-operative dungeon card game: each hero has only four action cards — Explore, Rest, Aid and Attack — rolled with custom dice; explore locations, fight enemies and race the peril track across a five-quest campaign.",
su=["Choose a quest; build location, enemy and loot decks per the quest sheet.","Each player picks a hero (Ironbreaker, Warrior Priest, Bright Wizard, Waywatcher) with 4 action cards; fewer players means more hit points; solo usually runs 2 heroes.","Place the peril token, choose a party leader, reveal the first location and spawn enemies."],
t=["Hero phase: each hero performs 1 action — Explore (progress tokens), Rest (heal), Aid (give success tokens to another hero, max 2 per card) or Attack (damage an engaged enemy; ranged can hit shadows).","Used action cards are exhausted; one action per hero readies all of them.","Every action you take triggers a black die from each enemy engaged with you.","Enemy phase, then location phase (resolve effects; travel when fully explored), then the peril token advances."],
e=["Complete the quest's final objective (e.g. defeat the nemesis) to win as a team.","Lose if all heroes are defeated or a quest failure condition triggers.","In campaign mode heroes level up between quests."],
tp=["Kill high-attack enemies before exploring.","Aid tokens on a teammate's key action are strong.","Plan your ready timing."],
pf=["Each engaged enemy rolls a black die whenever you act.","Max 2 success tokens per action card.","3-player: first player acts twice; 2-player: each acts twice."]),
161:dict(n="Cthulhu's Pact (K's Board Games 7)",s="Seventh title in the K's Board Games line: a Cthulhu-themed scheming party card game where cultists plot during the ritual — only the most devout are favoured. 4–6 players, 15–20 minutes. Full written rules are not public.",
su=["Read every card type aloud before the first game."],
t=["Play per the rulebook; expect fast take-that style interaction."],
e=["Win per the rulebook."],
tp=["More players means more chaos and laughs.","Watch who is targeting you."],
pf=["Detailed rules not found online; follow the rulebook."]),
162:dict(n="Apocalypse Revelation (zombie survival co-op)",s="Small-box American-style co-op: each character has a personal deck; each round roll for monster spawns, draw, take 4 actions (move, draw, play, card action, scavenge) and complete the scenario. An empty deck means death.",
su=["Choose a scenario and lay out map tiles in a grid face down as it requires.","Prepare scavenge and monster decks.","Each player takes a character and its deck and draws 4 cards; set the hunger die to 1."],
t=["Monster spawn: roll 2d6; every revealed tile whose number equals the sum spawns monsters.","Draw 1 card from your own deck (hand limit 10).","Take exactly 4 actions: move 1 tile (reveal unexplored tiles), draw, play a card (gear limit 4), take a card action, or scavenge.","Resolve location effects; then engaged monsters attack you."],
e=["Complete the scenario objective to win together.","If a character dies (no health, or deck runs out) the game is normally lost."],
tp=["Avoid tiles with frequently rolled numbers.","Draw to find weapons, but watch your deck size.","Combine play-a-card with a card action for combos."],
pf=["Exactly 4 actions per player.","An empty deck kills your character.","Stealth check: stealth minus the 2d6 modifier must reach the number of monster tokens."]),
163:dict(n="Magic Awakening (K's Board Games)",s="Magic-themed party card game from the K's Board Games line (box top: \"Welcome to the Magic World\"). No written rules were found online.",
su=["Read the whole rules sheet first."],
t=["Play per the rulebook; check whether victory is individual or team-based."],
e=["Win per the rulebook."],
tp=["A quick filler for after dinner."],
pf=["Data incomplete — follow the rulebook."]),
164:dict(n="Legendary Encounters: Alien",s="Co-operative deck-builder: use Attack to scan and kill aliens advancing from the Hive, use Recruit to buy cards from the Barracks, and complete three film-based objectives. Facehuggers burst out after two turns.",
su=["Build three objective mini-decks (9, 11 and 13 cards), each with one Drone per player.","Shuffle the Barracks (4 characters × 14 cards) and reveal 5 in HQ.","Each player shuffles 7 Specialists, 5 Grunts and 1 Role card and draws 6."],
t=["Play cards for Attack and Recruit points and their effects.","Scan face-down Hive cards in the Complex, or attack revealed aliens in the Combat Zone.","Recruit from HQ (refill immediately).","Hive phase: a new Hive card enters and pushes the others forward; Strike phase: aliens in the Combat Zone hit the active player. Discard and draw 6."],
e=["Win by completing all three objectives in order.","Lose if any player is killed (base rules) or another objective failure condition triggers."],
tp=["Scan before committing attacks.","Do not let the Combat Zone fill up.","Split roles between attackers and recruiters."],
pf=["Facehuggers burst after 2 turns.","Base rules: one death loses the game for everyone.","Gory theme, 17+."]),
165:dict(n="MOMONEY",s="Chinese Monopoly-style game, electronic banking edition (card reader instead of paper money) with a dice tower: roll around the board, buy property, collect rent, build and bankrupt opponents. Rules follow common Monopoly practice; check the rulebook.",
su=["Each player takes a token and starting money (loaded onto their bank card in the electronic version).","The bank holds the property cards; check the card reader's batteries."],
t=["Roll two dice and move.","Unowned property: buy it (or auction per the rulebook); owned property: pay rent; complete colour sets to build houses and hotels.","Chance / Community-style spaces: draw a card; pass Start: collect salary; jail per the rulebook."],
e=["Last player not bankrupt wins, or compare total assets at an agreed time limit."],
tp=["Build only after completing a colour set.","Agree a time limit."],
pf=["Card-reader payments are slow — both players should check the amount.","Exact rules depend on the box."]),
166:dict(n="Age of War",s="Reiner Knizia's feudal-Japan dice game: roll 7 dice and fill one battle line on a castle card per roll; if you cannot, lose a die and reroll. Conquer castles, steal them, and unite clans for big points.",
su=["Lay all 14 castle cards (6 clans) face up in the centre.","Put the 7 dice nearby; choose a first player."],
t=["Roll all 7 dice and choose one castle to attack (centre, or an opponent's unprotected castle).","After each roll you must complete exactly one battle line with matching dice; then reroll the rest.","If you cannot complete a line, set one die aside and reroll.","Complete every line to take the card; run out of dice and the attack fails. Stealing needs the extra red daimyo line."],
e=["The game ends when the last centre castle is taken.","Score castles, or the higher clan value for each united clan (united clans cannot be stolen); highest total wins."],
tp=["Fill hard lines (cavalry, archers, daimyo) first and infantry last.","Finish clans before rivals steal from them.","Late game: steal or take a cheap centre castle?"],
pf=["One castle per turn.","Infantry lines count total infantry; several dice can combine.","Only united clans are protected."]),
}
